/T (Tai Tanzania screening Elimika na Mwajuma in their workshop in Shinyanga. During physical outreach visits to four wards in Kahama municipality, Shinyanga region, 355 adolescent girls and young women were reached. The project beneficiaries ranged in age from 12 to 29, with the youngest being 12 and the oldest being 29. In terms of education, the majority of beneficiaries were in secondary school. About 27 women said they had gotten pregnant at least once, and the majority of them said it happened before they were 18.)
/E (Tai Tanzania screening Elimika na Mwajuma in their workshop in Shinyanga. During physical outreach visits to four wards in Kahama municipality, Shinyanga region, 355 adolescent girls and young women were reached. The project beneficiaries ranged in age from 12 to 29, with the youngest being 12 and the oldest being 29. In terms of education, the majority of beneficiaries were in secondary school. About 27 women said they had gotten pregnant at least once, and the majority of them said it happened before they were 18.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
