/P 139 0 R
/E (In March 2022, we launched a social media outreach programme featuring different social change makers to discuss prevelant issues affecting children, youth, and women in our communities. We have held seven sessions via Instagram live and Twitter spaces with a total of 346 participants. The English-Swahili sessions provide us with the opportunity to engage in real-time conversations with our intended beneficiaries, experts, and government officials. The atmosphere created during these sessions is conducive to productive experiences, allowing us to bounce ideas off each other while simultaneously learning facts about violence against women and children. Through these sessions, we gain a deeper understanding of the scope of the issue and explore ways to prevent it.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
